-- GENERATED by scripts/build-patra-pushpa-pairings.mjs. Do not hand-edit.
--
-- Closes the oldest open question in docs/sources.md: the 21 leaves are paired
-- with 21 names, 14 of the pairs alliterate, and the other 7 looked mismatched.
--
-- The alliteration IS the design -- but only ONE of the seven is an error here.
-- The other six are paired the same way in the book, deliberately. The seventh:
--   bhRngaraajatkaTaaya namaha -> ashvattha patram     (this app)
--   bhRngaraajatkaTaaya namaha -> bhRngaraaja patram   (the book)
-- A name meaning "he whose matted hair is the bhringaraja" was getting a peepal
-- leaf.
--
-- Four more differences alliteration would never have caught, plus the order:
-- the app had Ekadanta/daaDimee at 12 where the book has it at 21. And two in
-- the flowers, of which shamyaaka -> shyaamaka is the clearest transcription
-- error found in this project: the same four syllables in a different order.
--
-- Idempotent.
-- =============================================================================

